{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba PAID-GATE.md | sed -n '228,245p'; nl -ba paid_rehearsal.py | sed -n '444,473p;596,619p'; rg -n 'retries.jsonl|63 of|33 of' rehearsal.log paid-mutants.log\"","aggregated_output":"   228\t## 3h. After council round 47g (`codex-r47g.md`)\n   229\t\n   230\t- **[47g] Two journals, read on the writer's own delimiter.**\n   231\t  - Scored first attempts are written to `answers.jsonl`, and diagnostic retries to `retries.jsonl`. The run digest covers both.\n   232\t  - A damaged line in `answers.jsonl` makes the verdict INCOMPLETE. A damaged line in `retries.jsonl` is reported and marks that retry\n   233\t    interrupted, but leaves the scored test complete.\n   234\t  - Records are split on '\\n' only, the writer's delimiter. An answer may contain other Unicode line separators (U+2028, U+0085,\n   235\t    U+2029), and these are kept inside the record.\n   236\t  - Rehearsed: a torn retry record leaves the verdict complete; a torn scored record (the existing control) makes it INCOMPLETE; an\n   237\t    answer holding U+2028, U+0085 and U+2029 stays one record; the order of every first attempt before any retry is checked on the\n   238\t    provider's own call sequence.\n   239\t- **Rehearsal:** 63 of 63, three runs (`rehearsal.log`).\n   240\t- **Mutants:** 33 of 33 caught, and the control passes (`paid-mutants.log`).\n   241\t  - One mutant (splitting on any line break) is caught when a scenario guard stops the rehearsal: 36 attempts started, 35 finished.\n   242\t  - The mutant harness now counts such a stop as a catch and shows its reason.\n   243\t\n   244\t## 4. The reading rule (fixed now, before any answer exists)\n   245\t\n   444\t    tfrozen = json.loads((tkeys / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   445\t    rd = {pid: {c: card() for c in k['cards']} for pid, k in pg.render_packets(scratch / 'one-transport', tfrozen)[1].items()}\n   446\t    v = verdict_of(rd, 'transport', out=scratch / 'one-transport', keys=tkeys, packets_sha=pg.hashlib.sha256((scratch / 'one-transport' / 'packets.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n   447\t    check('verdict: a unit failed in transport makes the verdict INCOMPLETE', v['verdict'] == 'INCOMPLETE'\n   448\t          and any('single-E|single|1: transport' in x for x in v['problems']), '; '.join(v['problems'][:2]))\n   449\t\n   450\t\n   451\t    def read_all(folder, keys):\n   452\t        pg.packets(scratch / folder, keys)\n   453\t        kf = json.loads((keys / 'packet-key.json').read_text())\n   454\t        rend = pg.render_packets(scratch / folder, kf)[1]\n   455\t        rd = {pid: {c: card() for c in k['cards']} for pid, k in rend.items()}\n   456\t        return verdict_of(rd, folder, out=scratch / folder, keys=keys,\n   457\t                          packets_sha=pg.hashlib.sha256((scratch / folder / 'packets.md').read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n   458\t\n   459\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'interrupt', interrupted=True)\n   460\t    f = s['finals']\n   461\t    v = read_all('interrupt', scratch / 'key-interrupt')\n   462\t    check('interrupt during a scored attempt: results written; that attempt interrupted, later ones not sent, no retry yet; INCOMPLETE',\n   463\t          (scratch / 'interrupt' / 'results.json').exists() and f['single-O|single|2']['decision'] == 'interrupted'\n   464\t          and f['single-S|single|2']['decision'] == 'not sent' and f['single-O|single|1']['decision'] == 'retry not sent'\n   465\t          and f['pair-old-1|joint|1']['decision'] == 'publish' and v['verdict'] == 'INCOMPLETE', '; '.join(v['problems'][:2]))\n   466\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'interrupt-retry', interrupted=True)\n   467\t    f = s['finals']\n   468\t    v = read_all('interrupt-retry', scratch / 'key-interrupt-retry')\n   469\t    firsts = [l for l in lines if l['attempt'] == 1]\n   470\t    check('interrupt during a diagnostic retry: all 36 scored attempts are recorded and the verdict is complete',\n   471\t          len(firsts) == 36 and f['single-O|single|1']['decision'] == 'interrupted' and pg.first_attempt(f['single-O|single|1'])['decision'] == 'refused'\n   472\t          and v['complete'], '; '.join(v['problems'][:2]))\n   473\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'retry-transport')\n   596\t    check('separate-unit: the same number in another unit is not unified (C4 refuses)', rec['decision'] == 'refused'\n   597\t          and any(c == 'C4' and 'forecast nodes' in m for c, m in rec['errors']) and not rec['calc']['unified'], rec['decision'])\n   598\t    # [47g] a damaged retry record stays diagnostic; Unicode separators inside an answer are not record breaks\n   599\t    shutil.copytree(scratch / 'retry', scratch / 'torn-retry', ignore=shutil.ignore_patterns('archives', 'packets.md', 'attempts.md', 'results.json'))\n   600\t    rpath = scratch / 'torn-retry' / 'retries.jsonl'\n   601\t    if not rpath.exists():\n   602\t        check('a damaged retry record is reported and the retry is interrupted, but the scored test stays complete', False, 'no retries journal')\n   603\t    else:\n   604\t        rj = rpath.read_text().split('\\n')[:-1]\n   605\t        rpath.write_text('\\n'.join(rj[:-1] + [rj[-1][:len(rj[-1]) // 2]]) + '\\n')\n   606\t        rs = pg.recover(scratch / 'torn-retry')\n   607\t        v = read_all('torn-retry', scratch / 'key-torn-retry')\n   608\t        check('a damaged retry record is reported and the retry is interrupted, but the scored test stays complete',\n   609\t              [d['journal'] for d in rs['damaged']] == ['retries.jsonl'] and rs['finals']['single-O|single|1']['decision'] == 'interrupted'\n   610\t              and v['complete'], '; '.join(v['problems'][:2]))\n   611\t    s, lines, stub, led = scenario(scratch, 'unicode')\n   612\t    v = read_all('unicode', scratch / 'key-unicode')\n   613\t    check('Unicode line separators inside an answer are kept in one record: the unit publishes and the verdict is complete',\n   614\t          '\\u2028' in (scratch / 'unicode' / 'answers.jsonl').read_text() and not s['damaged']\n   615\t          and s['finals']['single-O|single|1']['decision'] == 'publish' and v['complete'], '; '.join(v['problems'][:2]))\n   616\t    synthetic = scratch / 'retry-not-sent'\n   617\t    synthetic.mkdir()\n   618\t    base = {'unit': 'single-O', 'arm': 'single', 'draw': 1, 'attempt': 1}\n   619\t    (synthetic / 'answers.jsonl').write_text(json.dumps(dict(base, status='started')) + '\\n'\npaid-mutants.log:1:PASS  00 control  63 of 63 checks pass\npaid-mutants.log:35:33 of 33 mutants caught; control passes\nrehearsal.log:64:63 of 63 checks pass\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
